  "releaseNotes": "# AID v1.0.0 正式版\n\n## 中文发布说明\n\n### 核心能力\n\n- 正式发布 AI 漫剧创作能力，覆盖创意、剧本、角色、场景、道具、分镜、配音、视频生成和成片管理流程。\n- 正式发布 AI 电影项目化创作能力，支持电影项目、长叙事素材、多分镜任务、声音与画面资产以及成片流程的统一管理。\n- 正式发布 AI 漫画创作能力，支持角色、场景、道具、画风、分镜和漫画画面的结构化创作与资产复用。\n- 提供大语言、图片、视频和语音模型的统一接入、能力校验、任务调度、状态恢复、计费预冻结、结算与退款链路。\n- 提供用户、模型、服务商、计费、存储、登录方式、系统配置、运行配置和在线升级管理后台。\n\n### 新增与优化\n\n- 增加权威费用报价和结构化费用档位展示；生成前报价与正式提交共用模型解析、输入归一、SKU 命中和计费准备口径，只读报价不会创建任务、冻结余额或调用上游。\n- 增加可配置异步图片与视频协议、多参考图片/视频/音频装配、模型专属 LOGO，以及 Wan3.0、Agnes Video 2.5/Flash 等模型配置能力；新增模型默认停用，需完成凭证、权限和价格配置后再启用。\n- 剧本编辑支持正文哈希、自动保存、历史版本软删除和并发编辑保护；批量生成按项目、剧集与逻辑任务类型防止重复提交，并支持停止、续生和服务重启后的状态恢复。\n- 可配置异步视频协议支持音频开关字段与分辨率参数映射；后台提供结构化编辑和保存校验，兼容由上游隐式完成音画同步的模型。\n- Web 站点支持配置化品牌、Favicon、SEO、教程入口和匿名公共首页；模型选择及主要生成入口可在提交前展示确定或预估费用。\n- Web 加密请求使用稳定的服务端时差；请求时间戳过期时自动刷新公开配置、重新加密并安全重试一次。\n\n### 修复内容\n\n- 修复 Vidu 图片和视频模型的只读连通性探测使用非法任务 ID、遗漏识别结构化“任务不存在”响应而误报接口地址的问题。\n- 修复图片与视频任务的输入组合、规格、时长、比例、参考素材、音画能力和计费快照可能与真实上游请求不一致的问题。\n- 修复批量任务重复提交、组合链阶段绕过、停止后迟到结果回写、服务重启后任务槽恢复及部分生成进度无法正确结束的问题。\n- 修复模型参考音频配置、免费模型价格、SKU 计费口径、余额不足提示以及文本 Usage 分桶与结算中的多项一致性问题。\n- 修复剧本、分镜、资产导入、风格选择、生成历史、媒体预览和移动端访问中的多项交互与状态问题。\n\n### 部署与兼容性\n\n- 正式版使用 Java 17 运行环境，部署链固定使用 Oracle JDK 17.0.8；支持 Linux amd64 和 arm64。\n- 数据库基线为 MySQL 5.7；支持内置或外部 MySQL、Redis，可按配置启用 RocketMQ、HTTPS 和外部存储。\n- Docker 与非 Docker 部署均通过同一 `aid.sh` 管理安装、启动、停止、重启、升级、回滚、配置检查和卸载。\n- 本地媒体处理使用 AID 受管 FFmpeg 8.1.2 和中文字体稳定路径，安装与升级阶段执行版本、编码器、滤镜、字体和最小合成检查。\n- 在线源码构建按实时资源限制 CPU、内存和并行度，为宿主机保留至少 15% 可用资源；构建失败不会提前替换当前运行版本。\n- 国内环境优先使用 Gitee 与国内依赖节点，失败后回退 GitHub 或官方地址；所有固定运行时与升级器继续执行 SHA256 校验。\n\n### 数据库与升级说明\n\n- 全新安装统一使用 `sql/aid-init.sql`。\n- 从受支持测试版本升级时，升级器按 `aid_schema_history` 顺序执行尚未成功执行的增量 SQL；`sql/v1.0.0.sql` 为本次正式版幂等迁移入口，不新增表、字段或初始化数据。\n- 一键升级最低支持版本为 `v1.0.0-beta.5`。更早版本请先升级到受支持版本，或在备份数据后执行全新部署和数据迁移。\n- 升级前必须备份数据库、部署配置、证书和用户媒体目录；升级后请核验登录、存储、模型连接、计费、生成任务、FFmpeg 与中文字体能力。\n\n# AID v1.0.0 Stable Release\n\n## English Release Notes\n\n### Core Capabilities\n\n- Officially releases AI short-drama creation across ideation, scripts, characters, scenes, props, storyboards, dubbing, video generation, and final-output management.\n- Officially releases project-based AI film creation with unified management for long-form narrative assets, multi-shot tasks, audiovisual assets, and final production workflows.\n- Officially releases AI comic creation with structured characters, scenes, props, visual styles, storyboards, comic images, and reusable assets.\n- Provides unified LLM, image, video, and audio model integration with capability validation, task scheduling, recovery, billing pre-authorization, settlement, and refunds.\n- Provides administration for users, models, providers, billing, storage, sign-in channels, system settings, runtime configuration, and online upgrades.\n\n### Additions and Improvements\n\n- Added authoritative cost quotes and structured pricing tiers. Quotes and formal submissions share model resolution, normalized inputs, SKU matching, and billing preparation, while read-only quotes create no task, freeze no balance, and invoke no provider.\n- Added configurable asynchronous image and video protocols, multimodal reference assembly, per-model logos, and configuration support for Wan3.0 and Agnes Video 2.5/Flash. Newly added models remain disabled until credentials, permissions, and pricing are verified.\n- Added script content hashes, autosave, soft-deleted revision history, and concurrent-edit protection. Batch work is deduplicated by project, episode, and logical task type and remains recoverable across stop, resume, and service restarts.\n- Added configurable upstream audio-switch and resolution mappings for asynchronous video protocols, including structured admin editing and support for models that handle audiovisual synchronization implicitly.\n- Added configuration-driven branding, favicon, SEO, tutorial visibility, and anonymous public homepage data. Major generation entry points can show exact or estimated costs before submission.\n- Stabilized encrypted-request clock synchronization. Expired encrypted requests refresh public configuration, re-encrypt, and retry safely at most once.\n\n### Fixes\n\n- Fixed Vidu image and video read-only probes using invalid task identifiers and misclassifying structured task-not-found responses as endpoint failures.\n- Fixed inconsistencies between validated image/video inputs, task snapshots, billing inputs, and the media actually submitted upstream.\n- Fixed duplicate batch submissions, workflow-stage bypasses, late result writes after cancellation, restart recovery of task slots, and incomplete generation progress states.\n- Fixed multiple consistency issues in reference-audio configuration, free-model pricing, SKU metering, insufficient-balance errors, and text-usage settlement.\n- Fixed multiple interaction and state issues across scripts, storyboards, asset imports, style selection, generation history, media previews, and mobile access notices.\n\n### Deployment and Compatibility\n\n- Uses Java 17 with a fixed Oracle JDK 17.0.8 deployment runtime and supports Linux amd64 and arm64.\n- Uses MySQL 5.7 as the database baseline, with internal or external MySQL and Redis plus optional RocketMQ, HTTPS, and external object storage.\n- Docker and non-Docker deployments use the same `aid.sh` entry point for installation, start, stop, restart, upgrade, rollback, configuration checks, and uninstall.\n- Local media processing uses the managed FFmpeg 8.1.2 runtime and stable Chinese-font path, validated for version, encoders, filters, font coverage, and a minimal composition test during installation and upgrade.\n- Online source builds constrain CPU, memory, and parallelism from live capacity while reserving at least 15% for the host; a failed build does not replace the running version prematurely.\n- China-based deployments prefer Gitee and domestic dependency nodes, then fall back to GitHub or official sources. Fixed runtimes and updater artifacts remain protected by SHA256 verification.\n\n### Database and Upgrade Notes\n\n- Fresh installations use `sql/aid-init.sql` as the single initialization baseline.\n- Supported upgrades execute only successful-yet-unrecorded incremental SQL files in order through `aid_schema_history`. `sql/v1.0.0.sql` is the idempotent migration entry for this stable release and adds no tables, columns, or initialization data.\n- One-click upgrade requires at least `v1.0.0-beta.5`. Older installations must first move to a supported version or use a backed-up fresh deployment and controlled data migration.\n- Before upgrading, back up the database, deployment configuration, certificates, and user media. After upgrading, verify sign-in, storage, provider connectivity, billing, generation tasks, FFmpeg, and Chinese-font capabilities.",
